=== p2-windows · W7 · page:admin/SecretRotation (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:admin/SecretRotation   kind=page   web route=/admin/secret-rotation
Web source  : web/src/features/admin/pages/SecretRotationPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  SchemaDriftPage / VehicleCostPage / AuditLogPage do. The generated prompt's idealized
  "SecretRotationPage.xaml + SecretRotationPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Admin" is mapped onto these
  real conventions; the surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("SecretRotation",
  already in RouteTable.cs L216 -> /admin/secret-rotation) via ShellWindow.xaml.cs.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest data source is useSecretRotation (GET /admin/observability/secret-rotation,
  no params). The view-model reads through an injected ISecretRotationFeed; the default EmptySecretRotationFeed
  resolves the empty state, and the generated-client-backed SecretRotationClientFeed (SecretRotationPage.Source.cs)
  binds to the generated OpenAPI contract client operation get_api_v1_admin_observability_secret_rotation (confirmed
  in apps/windows/Generated/Api/ApiEndpoints.cs L51), asserted in tests via the FakeApiClient. The route is confirmed
  in internal/api/router.go ("GET /admin/observability/secret-rotation") and the wire shape in
  internal/rotation/tracker.go (rotation.Status: kind/target_id/last_rotated/age_days/expires_at/days_to_expiry/
  warn_days/critical_days/severity). No HTTP touches the view. A non-success response surfaces as ApiException; the
  view-model maps StatusCode==503 to the distinct subsystem-unavailable banner (web `subsystemMissing`) and every
  other failure to the generic InfoBar+Retry.
- The response is wrapped by the platform httputil.Respond envelope as {data:{items}} (the web hook unwraps via
  fetchEnvelope); SecretRotationSnapshot.FromJson unwraps the {data:…} envelope before reading the snake_case items[]
  so the wire shape round-trips losslessly (JsonReadHelpers reused from ApiLogsPage.Model.cs, same namespace).
- The web page renders its states INSIDE the PageContainer body, so the native port reproduces them as visible Fluent
  regions per ADR-006: loading -> TsStatGridSkeleton(4)+TsTableSkeleton shimmer; 503 subsystem-missing ->
  TsAlertBanner(Warning) notConfigured; generic error -> TsQueryError (InfoBar-equivalent) + Retry; success/empty
  content -> the overdue-rotations TsAlertBanner(Danger) (web counts.critical>0), the four tracked-secret TsStatCards
  (Tracked secrets / OK / Warn / Critical, gated on items.length>0 exactly like the web StatCard grid) and the
  rotation-status TsGlassPanel (web GlassPanel) hosting a custom Fluent Grid table — two-line kind / last-rotated /
  expiry cells + the right-aligned age / "Wd / Cd" thresholds + the severity TsBadge (web Badge) — or, when no
  rotation events recorded, a TsEmptyState. The table panel renders in BOTH success and empty (the body swaps to the
  EmptyState), never a blank region. The severity Badge + multi-line cells require the AuditLogPage-style custom Grid
  table; the shared TsDataTable only renders string cells, which would drop the chip + captions (a parity shortcut).
- SI units N/A (no unit-bearing physical fields on this admin surface — secret kinds, ISO instants and integer day
  counts/thresholds only). Counts + day values format through the shared NumberFormatting port at 0 decimals (web
  fmtNumber); the last-rotated/expiry instants through FormatDateTime (web formatDateTime full variant via
  DateTimeFormatting) + FormatRelative (web formatRelative tiers: just now / Nm / Nh / Nd ago, then absolute MMM d,
  yyyy), all at the display boundary.
- All 21 manifest i18n keys were added verbatim (web key names) to Strings/en/Resources.resw as
  translation.admin.secretRotation.* (20) + the reused translation.admin.subsystem.unavailableTitle (already
  present), alphabetically placed between admin.schemaDrift.* and admin.security.*; the three severity-chip labels
  (severityOk/severityWarn/severityCritical, web SEVERITY_LABEL) and the six kind labels (kindTeslaRefreshToken …,
  web KIND_LABELS) were added too so no literal is hardcoded (resolved but not counted in the 30; the unknown-tier
  chip + the no-target / no-expiry cells use the shared em-dash constant, matching the web '—'). The surface resolves
  every label through the ILocalizer facade. The ar/he catalogs lag en by design (translations land later); the app
  falls back to the English default via ILocalizer until translated.
- Microsoft.UI-free Model/Source/ViewModel links were added to TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj (the bare WinUI view is
  excluded — it uses Microsoft.UI), path-sorted between SchemaDriftPage and SecurityPanel.
- Build-time hygiene found + fixed in this surface's own new code (no red shipped): the five new C# files were
  authored with CRLF and the repo enforces LF via dotnet-format ENDOFLINE; all five were normalized to LF (UTF-8
  no-BOM) and re-verified clean. BuildRow was made static (no instance dependency, CA1822). The app + solution now
  build 0 errors and format verifies clean.

